                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "34184206",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197977397371",
                            "num_reviews": 19,
                            "playtime_forever": 582,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 582,
                            "last_played": 1497589715
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game has not recieved the love it deserves.\nThe unconvential approach demands that the play buy into the premise and approach of the game's design, and I will admit that the game does not really help you do so. Once I took the time to understand its premise, however, I thoroughly enjoyed it.\n\nThe most common critique of the game was the inability to save the game. This game is meant to be replayed, repeatedly to use the try new options, explore new paths, and further discover the story and details hiding in the dark corners. The different endings provide different bits of information, and some interestingly pleasantly experiences, should you take the time to see them through.\n\nI know it's hard to come to terms with, but you are not losing anything by the absence absence of a save feature. Each run is a new complete (and brief) experience. Once the map is familiar, speed runs take about 6 minutes (timed), and the world is not terribly large. It may have taken you a couple of hours to make it through the first to your first (non-suicide) ending, but future attempts do not take long at all, once you know the answers.\n\nThis game does not follow the format you're used to. Give it some time, expore the many ways to see the story through, and you will likely find this game a delightfully unique experience.",
